#: ../../.opencode/commands/prime.md:4
msgid ""
"Load session context. Do not begin any implementation — this is context-"
"only."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/prime.md:6
msgid ""
"**First, read your handoff briefing.** Run `hero next path` to get the "
"correct file path, then read it. This is a three-section briefing (Just "
"finished / Next / Context to carry forward) the previous session left "
"behind so you can resume without re-reading the chat. Surface its "
"contents to the user before any other priming output."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/prime.md:12
msgid ""
"In team mode, also check `.hero/NEXT.md` for the team roster (who's "
"working on what) and any recent team updates."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/prime.md:15
msgid ""
"**Then, surface the ready queue.** Read `.hero/QUEUE.md` (or run `hero "
"queue --limit 5`) and show the top few ready specs with their kickoff "
"prompts. This gives the user paste-ready session-openers for the parallel"
" work paths in flight, not just the one path NEXT.md captured. If the "
"queue is empty, skip silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/prime.md:21
msgid ""
"**Next, run `hero recap`** to get a spec-grouped summary of recent "
"activity (commits grouped by spec, status transitions, knowledge "
"updates). This complements the handoff — intent from the last session "
"plus facts from git. If there's no recent activity, skip this section "
"silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/prime.md:26
msgid ""
"**Then, auto-reconcile.** Run `hero check --reconcile` to fix any status "
"drift (specs stuck at delivering when git shows completion, etc.). This "
"prevents stale status from accumulating across sessions. If nothing needs"
" fixing, skip silently."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/prime.md:31
msgid ""
"Then be the `session-primer` agent and orient the engineer on active "
"work, conventions, decisions, and risks."
msgstr ""

#: ../../.opencode/commands/prime.md:34
msgid "Session context: $ARGUMENTS"
msgstr ""

